1
00:00:34,959 --> 00:00:35,999
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:35,999 --> 00:00:37,029
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,029 --> 00:00:38,102
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:38,102 --> 00:00:40,295
[Episode 7]

5
00:00:42,791 --> 00:00:46,054
[Jaejae Noodles]

6
00:00:48,232 --> 00:00:50,504
- Going for a run again?
- Yeah.

7
00:00:50,504 --> 00:00:53,054
Why are you running in the middle of the night?

8
00:00:53,054 --> 00:00:54,946
So I don't run into him.

9
00:00:54,946 --> 00:00:56,333
You mean Soo Bin?

10
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:58,921
Is that why you've been working from home?

11
00:00:58,921 --> 00:01:01,131
See? I told you.

12
00:01:01,131 --> 00:01:03,206
I knew I was right.

13
00:01:03,206 --> 00:01:05,249
Only a man knows...

14
00:01:05,249 --> 00:01:09,039
what's on another man's mind.

15
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:11,308
Yeah! You're right!

16
00:01:11,308 --> 00:01:12,883
Dead right!

17
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:14,767
- Darn it!
- Ugh...

18
00:01:15,661 --> 00:01:17,639
Ah, it's dead!

19
00:01:29,279 --> 00:01:32,075
[Revised Script for Gyeongseong Love Song]
<i>Sending the revised script.</i>

20
00:01:32,075 --> 00:01:34,732
Finally, I have an excuse to see her...

21
00:01:39,478 --> 00:01:40,905
I guess I still haven't moved on.

22
00:01:40,905 --> 00:01:44,701
Mister, focus!

23
00:01:45,516 --> 00:01:47,938
- Here!
- Thank you.

24
00:01:51,461 --> 00:01:53,540
Give it to me. I'll open it for you.

25
00:01:55,306 --> 00:01:58,098
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

26
00:01:58,801 --> 00:02:02,168
- It came out!
- Oh, did you get it?

27
00:02:05,535 --> 00:02:07,252
I really miss her...

28
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:08,495
Who are you talking about?

29
00:02:08,495 --> 00:02:11,740
- Oh... my colleague?
- Your colleague?

30
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,484
Well...

31
00:02:13,484 --> 00:02:15,738
- My friend.
- I do know it.

32
00:02:15,738 --> 00:02:19,517
I just thought it was weird
to miss a colleague.

33
00:02:19,517 --> 00:02:20,768
Why is that weird?

34
00:02:20,768 --> 00:02:25,008
They say missing someone means you love them.

35
00:02:25,008 --> 00:02:28,732
It's hard to love a colleague, isn't it?

36
00:02:28,732 --> 00:02:31,754
You're pretty smart.

37
00:02:31,754 --> 00:02:33,731
- You take after your mom, don't you?
- Yep.

38
00:02:33,731 --> 00:02:38,751
They say I got my mom's brains
and my dad's face.

39
00:02:38,751 --> 00:02:40,248
Sounds about right.

40
00:02:40,248 --> 00:02:42,714
Kim Seong Chan! Daddy's here!

41
00:02:42,714 --> 00:02:44,259
Daddy!

42
00:02:44,259 --> 00:02:46,938
- Daddy!
- Oh, look who's here!

43
00:02:46,938 --> 00:02:49,196
Come here. Oh, my baby!

44
00:02:49,196 --> 00:02:51,203
- Did you have fun with him?
- Yes.

45
00:02:51,203 --> 00:02:52,930
Oh, dear... oh, my.

46
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:54,328
Sorry about that.

47
00:02:54,328 --> 00:02:57,214
A big group came into Mom's restaurant.

48
00:02:57,214 --> 00:02:58,866
It's fine. It wasn't long.

49
00:02:58,866 --> 00:03:00,809
- I'll buy you a drink next time.
- It's fine.

50
00:03:00,809 --> 00:03:02,974
Say goodbye, Seong Chan.

51
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:06,629
- Yeah. Bye, Seung Chan.
- It's Seong Chan.

52
00:03:06,629 --> 00:03:10,944
Yeah, Seung Chan. See you next time.

53
00:03:10,944 --> 00:03:12,365
[Kim Seong Chan]

54
00:03:13,356 --> 00:03:15,991
Let's go, come here. Oh, dear.

55
00:03:15,991 --> 00:03:17,965
- Bye.
- Yeah, see you.

56
00:03:17,965 --> 00:03:20,012
- See you!
- Bye!

57
00:03:20,012 --> 00:03:24,296
Aw, you're such a cutie. Come on, let's go.

58
00:03:25,787 --> 00:03:27,860
He's such a good dad.

59
00:03:30,603 --> 00:03:32,359
Grandma, Mom!

60
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:33,663
I brought twist donuts.

61
00:03:33,663 --> 00:03:35,916
We're already eating.

62
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:38,291
Yi Jae stopped by earlier.

63
00:03:38,291 --> 00:03:40,466
Why haven't you two been hanging out lately?

64
00:03:40,466 --> 00:03:44,439
Oh, we've been working separately.

65
00:03:45,666 --> 00:03:48,204
By the way, what are you two doing?

66
00:03:48,204 --> 00:03:53,434
I'm studying for the written driver's test,
and Grandma's studying Korean!

67
00:03:53,434 --> 00:03:55,092
You're getting your driver's license?

68
00:03:55,092 --> 00:03:57,920
It's about time I learned to go places
on my own.

69
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,010
And you'll go places with me too.

70
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:03,014
I should teach you how to drive.

71
00:04:03,014 --> 00:04:05,477
They say you should never learn
driving from family.

72
00:04:05,477 --> 00:04:08,318
There! Look at this.

73
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:11,737
[Park Jong Sun, Lee Hwa Yeon, Woo Soo Min]
I don't know everything yet,

74
00:04:11,737 --> 00:04:13,826
but I've got these memorized.

75
00:04:13,826 --> 00:04:16,582
Wow, even Mom's and my names?

76
00:04:16,582 --> 00:04:19,428
You'll be writing poetry before long.

77
00:04:20,581 --> 00:04:22,690
But...

78
00:04:22,690 --> 00:04:24,257
Like this... and like this.

79
00:04:24,257 --> 00:04:29,147
Oh, it's "bieup!" I knew that!

80
00:04:29,147 --> 00:04:31,146
"Bin."

81
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,162
You never make mistakes.

82
00:04:33,162 --> 00:04:36,311
You must've gotten nervous
because Soo Bin's here.

83
00:04:36,311 --> 00:04:37,527
Oh, my...

84
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,461
- "Bin!"
- "Bin."

85
00:04:39,461 --> 00:04:41,221
It's done, right?

86
00:04:54,293 --> 00:04:55,762
Mr. Kim?

87
00:04:55,762 --> 00:04:57,715
You can't just park here out
in the open like this.

88
00:04:57,715 --> 00:04:59,907
Madam's here, isn't she?

89
00:04:59,907 --> 00:05:02,060
Sir told me to bring her back.

90
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,859
If he misses her that much,
tell him to come himself.

91
00:05:04,859 --> 00:05:06,830
Soo Bin!

92
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:20,382
If you come again, I'll report you.

93
00:05:20,382 --> 00:05:23,424
Soo Bin! Soo Bin...

94
00:05:23,424 --> 00:05:25,640
Okay, is everyone here?

95
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,493
Please put it up on the screen...

96
00:05:28,493 --> 00:05:30,227
And here comes Mr. Game Changer.

97
00:05:30,227 --> 00:05:31,712
[Love Chain, The 7th Chain Mate Enters]

98
00:05:36,781 --> 00:05:40,267
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

99
00:05:40,267 --> 00:05:42,621
Hello...

100
00:05:42,621 --> 00:05:45,208
Oh, me too...

101
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:47,830
- Oh!
- Oh!

102
00:05:47,830 --> 00:05:50,116
- Please, have a seat wherever you'd like.
- Please have a seat.

103
00:05:50,116 --> 00:05:52,279
- Oh, sure.
- Yeah, where would you like to...

104
00:05:52,279 --> 00:05:54,963
Yeah, all the full shots look good,
and Camera 34 pan left...

105
00:05:54,963 --> 00:05:56,329
- and stay on the Game Changer.
- Sa Rang!

106
00:05:56,329 --> 00:06:00,267
Amazing! The vibe changed when he walked in.

107
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:01,829
Isn't it amazing?

108
00:06:01,829 --> 00:06:04,664
Yes, yes. It looks good now...

109
00:06:04,664 --> 00:06:08,562
Let's get the men's group shots
and reactions next.

110
00:06:08,562 --> 00:06:10,198
Yeah.

111
00:06:10,198 --> 00:06:12,330
- The Game Changer is getting a great reaction.
<i>- First impression...</i>

112
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:13,713
- Yeah, good.
<i>- Well...</i>

113
00:06:13,713 --> 00:06:16,472
- The audio is picking up well, right?
<i>- For now, I'll just wait and see...</i>

114
00:06:16,472 --> 00:06:20,495
Production team, do the interviews first,
then check the outdoor setup one more time.

115
00:06:20,495 --> 00:06:24,073
- Yes, looks good.
<i>- There's sliced bread over there too.</i>

116
00:06:24,073 --> 00:06:26,560
<i>Grapes and egg tarts...</i>

117
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:44,938
Boss, Yu Geon acts that way
because he feels guilty toward you.

118
00:06:45,635 --> 00:06:48,815
And you act that way
because you love him. Right?

119
00:06:50,258 --> 00:06:53,091
Still, Yu Geon is pretty frustrating too.

120
00:06:53,091 --> 00:06:57,211
All he has to do is ask
my sister or Soo Bin to cast him.

121
00:06:57,211 --> 00:06:59,997
I wonder who he got that stubbornness from...

122
00:07:05,370 --> 00:07:07,239
He got it from me.

123
00:07:07,239 --> 00:07:09,005
I was the same.

124
00:07:09,005 --> 00:07:11,682
All because of my stupid pride...

125
00:07:12,659 --> 00:07:15,209
I couldn't even ask anyone for help...

126
00:07:32,133 --> 00:07:34,879
Oh? Mister! Hello.

127
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:37,505
Hey, Soo Bin. It's been a while.

128
00:07:37,505 --> 00:07:41,319
Uh... is Yi Jae here with you?

129
00:07:41,319 --> 00:07:44,384
No, it's just me right now.

130
00:07:44,384 --> 00:07:46,947
Oh, I see...

131
00:07:46,947 --> 00:07:50,717
- Would you like to come in for a moment?
- No, never mind.

132
00:07:50,717 --> 00:07:53,811
Well, the reason I'm here is...

133
00:07:53,811 --> 00:07:57,530
I wanted you and Yi Jae to take a look at this.

134
00:07:57,530 --> 00:07:58,565
What's this?

135
00:07:58,565 --> 00:08:00,692
Don't feel pressured. Got it?

136
00:08:00,692 --> 00:08:03,335
- Oh...
- See you.

137
00:08:03,335 --> 00:08:07,267
- No, sir, this...
- Yeah, yeah. Go on inside.

138
00:08:15,692 --> 00:08:16,748
[Yu Geon's Dream]

139
00:08:16,748 --> 00:08:19,499
[Bus No. 31 (Mail Carrier)]
[Letter from That Day (Post Office Employee 3)]

140
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:22,377
[Witness for the Shadows (Court Clerk)]
[Fishing King (Student 2)]

141
00:08:25,467 --> 00:08:28,959
You've really worked hard, Sim Yu Geon.

142
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:30,417
[Sending the revised script]

143
00:08:30,417 --> 00:08:31,700
[Thank you]
[Thank you for your hard work]

144
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:34,378
He read it, but didn't say a word.

145
00:08:35,634 --> 00:08:36,655
[Woo Soo Bin]

146
00:08:38,747 --> 00:08:40,066
Why's he calling?

147
00:08:40,066 --> 00:08:41,630
No...

148
00:08:42,379 --> 00:08:44,232
It'll look like I've been
waiting for him to call.

149
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,591
But I have! Right?

150
00:08:46,591 --> 00:08:48,918
I've been waiting for feedback!

151
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:54,568
Yeah?

152
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:57,119
Yeah, now?

153
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:58,524
Oh, to your studio?

154
00:08:58,524 --> 00:09:01,624
Oh, now? Well...

155
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:03,768
It might take a while...

156
00:09:03,768 --> 00:09:07,689
Okay, see you later. Yeah.

157
00:09:08,751 --> 00:09:11,213
That was incredibly natural.

158
00:09:13,231 --> 00:09:14,880
Well...

159
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:18,335
Being colleagues isn't so hard after all!

160
00:09:27,702 --> 00:09:30,231
Oh, I was wondering who it was.

161
00:09:30,231 --> 00:09:32,930
- You could've just come in.
- It's called manners.

162
00:09:32,930 --> 00:09:34,649
Yeah...

163
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:37,687
Oh...

164
00:09:37,687 --> 00:09:39,494
you...

165
00:09:40,205 --> 00:09:42,165
Well...

166
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:44,874
- I'll go this way.
- Oh, okay.

167
00:09:49,687 --> 00:09:51,719
[10 Reasons Contract Marriage Is Dangerous]
<i>Go with Plan B!</i>

168
00:10:00,539 --> 00:10:03,454
Wow... even his latest drama is here?

169
00:10:03,454 --> 00:10:04,830
Mister gave you all this?

170
00:10:04,830 --> 00:10:06,389
It's a little over an hour long.

171
00:10:06,389 --> 00:10:08,827
Has it already been an hour?

172
00:10:08,827 --> 00:10:10,602
Time flies.

173
00:10:10,602 --> 00:10:14,074
Waiting for you felt longer...

174
00:10:14,074 --> 00:10:15,573
Huh?

175
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:17,451
Oh, well...

176
00:10:19,995 --> 00:10:23,152
Well, I guess it's because
Yu Geon's such a good actor.

177
00:10:24,908 --> 00:10:28,249
Exactly... that's what I meant.

178
00:10:28,249 --> 00:10:30,484
Then maybe there's something
Yu Geon could do...

179
00:10:30,484 --> 00:10:34,370
- Even a small role...
- Yeah, even a small role would be good.

180
00:10:35,951 --> 00:10:37,835
- No, I don't want to give him one.
- Huh?

181
00:10:37,835 --> 00:10:40,904
I don't want to throw him scraps like,
"Here, take this."

182
00:10:40,904 --> 00:10:43,268
It's disrespectful to Yu Geon.

183
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:45,070
Let him audition.

184
00:10:45,070 --> 00:10:47,508
But if I bring him in,
he'll probably refuse to come.

185
00:10:47,508 --> 00:10:50,369
If he gets it, it'll feel awkward.
If he doesn't, he'll be disappointed.

186
00:10:50,369 --> 00:10:52,999
Then it would be better
to reach out through his agency.

187
00:10:52,999 --> 00:10:54,385
He doesn't have an agency.

188
00:10:54,385 --> 00:10:56,438
What? Then he's been doing all this on his own?

189
00:10:56,438 --> 00:10:59,141
Having an agency makes a huge difference.

190
00:10:59,141 --> 00:11:01,722
You don't even get
the same audition opportunities.

191
00:11:01,722 --> 00:11:03,804
Oh, jeez...

192
00:11:03,804 --> 00:11:05,480
I don't get it.

193
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:09,345
Does he think actors with that face
and that level of talent are common?

194
00:11:09,345 --> 00:11:11,576
Uh... well...

195
00:11:14,506 --> 00:11:15,508
What?

196
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:20,297
You've always loved his face.
Enough to make me jealous.

197
00:11:20,297 --> 00:11:22,516
I was the jealous one.

198
00:11:22,516 --> 00:11:25,678
You were the one who said
Yu Geon has a face the camera can't resist.

199
00:11:25,678 --> 00:11:28,889
When did I say that? I filmed you a lot more.

200
00:11:28,889 --> 00:11:31,298
- Huh?
- Oh...

201
00:11:31,298 --> 00:11:35,570
Well, that makes sense. We were dating...

202
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:36,852
Oh...

203
00:11:36,852 --> 00:11:38,839
That's all in the past.

204
00:11:38,839 --> 00:11:42,160
- I just can't resist filming beautiful...
- Huh?

205
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,555
Oh...

206
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,747
Well, then... I should go.

207
00:11:51,747 --> 00:11:52,854
Where are you going?

208
00:11:52,854 --> 00:11:57,327
- Huh? What?
- We still have to go over the revised script.

209
00:11:57,327 --> 00:11:58,868
Oh.

210
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,751
Here? O-over there?

211
00:12:05,751 --> 00:12:07,667
- Yeah.
- Should we do it there?

212
00:12:08,968 --> 00:12:10,560
Here? Oh...

213
00:12:17,784 --> 00:12:20,622
[An Su Hui]
[Sim Yu Geon]

214
00:12:24,619 --> 00:12:27,387
<i>Why are you offering me a contract like this?</i>

215
00:12:28,009 --> 00:12:30,601
<i>It seems like I have nothing to lose.</i>

216
00:12:31,716 --> 00:12:34,513
<i>You've already lost the most important thing.</i>

217
00:12:34,513 --> 00:12:37,037
<i>I bought your heart.</i>

218
00:12:37,037 --> 00:12:39,596
<i>So you'll never fall in love with Ha Na.</i>

219
00:12:39,596 --> 00:12:43,037
<i>- I never had those feelings to begin with.
- Of course, you don't. I took them.</i>

220
00:12:43,037 --> 00:12:45,332
<i>And you'd better keep it that way.</i>

221
00:12:46,566 --> 00:12:48,043
<i>Isn't it funny?</i>

222
00:12:48,043 --> 00:12:53,239
<i>That a single piece of paper can bind
both your body and your heart.</i>

223
00:13:00,737 --> 00:13:02,787
Wow...

224
00:13:05,568 --> 00:13:07,122
Wow...

225
00:13:07,122 --> 00:13:10,927
I like people like you, who show results
right away when you invest in them.

226
00:13:10,927 --> 00:13:13,795
Makes spending money worthwhile. Get in.

227
00:13:37,263 --> 00:13:41,122
No. You should sit next to me. Right here.

228
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:43,312
Oh...

229
00:13:48,501 --> 00:13:50,698
Is someone else joining us?

230
00:13:52,569 --> 00:13:55,532
- Oh.
- Oh, you're already here.

231
00:13:59,388 --> 00:14:01,281
Sim Yu Geon!

232
00:14:02,634 --> 00:14:04,307
Soo Bin.

233
00:14:05,523 --> 00:14:08,491
Oh, you know each other?

234
00:14:08,491 --> 00:14:10,733
Perfect.

235
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:13,785
Maybe we'll make it to the gym
before it closes after all.

236
00:14:14,858 --> 00:14:18,548
Looks like you're really happy
to see him here, huh, Ian?

237
00:14:18,548 --> 00:14:20,202
What do you want?

238
00:14:20,202 --> 00:14:24,769
What does it look like?
I want him to play Moo Gyeom.

239
00:14:30,225 --> 00:14:31,713
What?

240
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,099
You've really outdone yourself.

241
00:14:36,099 --> 00:14:38,898
First you created an audition
that wasn't even planned,

242
00:14:38,898 --> 00:14:40,779
and now you're telling us who to cast?

243
00:14:40,779 --> 00:14:42,920
As the lead, no less?

244
00:14:44,559 --> 00:14:48,166
Director Ian, don't block the doorway.
Come sit down.

245
00:14:48,166 --> 00:14:50,006
You too.

246
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:54,380
Sim Yu Geon, come outside.

247
00:15:00,837 --> 00:15:02,947
Aren't you coming out?

248
00:15:14,568 --> 00:15:16,865
Looks like we're not making it
to the gym today.

249
00:15:23,896 --> 00:15:26,190
What are you doing here?

250
00:15:26,190 --> 00:15:29,682
Yi Jae was even hesitant
to suggest you audition.

251
00:15:29,682 --> 00:15:32,331
I guess we worried for nothing.

252
00:15:32,331 --> 00:15:35,226
You should've just asked Yi Jae or me.

253
00:15:35,226 --> 00:15:38,124
That would've been much easier.

254
00:15:38,124 --> 00:15:42,920
This is easier than becoming
a burden to the people I care about.

255
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,444
So this is what you chose instead?

256
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:48,291
I didn't know I'd run into you.

257
00:15:48,991 --> 00:15:50,727
I'm sorry.

258
00:15:53,343 --> 00:15:55,057
If you were going to get in
through connections anyway,

259
00:15:55,057 --> 00:15:57,917
you should've done it back
when you were young enough to be naive.

260
00:15:57,917 --> 00:16:00,588
After everything you've put yourself through...

261
00:16:01,256 --> 00:16:02,919
now, of all times?

262
00:16:03,589 --> 00:16:05,638
What do you know?

263
00:16:05,638 --> 00:16:07,548
You have no idea what it took
for me to make it this far.

264
00:16:07,548 --> 00:16:10,219
So don't act like you know
what I've been through.

265
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,806
You think I should've done it when I was naive?

266
00:16:14,668 --> 00:16:17,969
I did the best I could back then...

267
00:16:18,889 --> 00:16:21,409
and this is the best I can do now.

268
00:16:22,607 --> 00:16:24,060
Yeah.

269
00:16:24,994 --> 00:16:26,197
But...

270
00:16:26,197 --> 00:16:28,572
look at yourself in the mirror.

271
00:16:28,572 --> 00:16:31,561
Does this look like
the face of someone doing his best?

272
00:16:33,627 --> 00:16:35,403
Sim Yu Geon.

273
00:16:36,012 --> 00:16:40,458
I may not have liked you that much,
but I always thought you had a certain charm.

274
00:16:41,091 --> 00:16:44,747
But, right now... you're not.

275
00:16:59,109 --> 00:17:00,703
Ian!

276
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:03,363
Wait!

277
00:17:03,363 --> 00:17:05,054
Hey, you...

278
00:17:06,990 --> 00:17:09,135
You're just leaving like this?

279
00:17:09,135 --> 00:17:12,453
Calm down and hear me out.

280
00:17:12,453 --> 00:17:14,614
You crossed the line too.

281
00:17:14,614 --> 00:17:18,118
At least back then with Oh Ha Na,
you had the decency to go behind my back.

282
00:17:18,118 --> 00:17:22,237
He was going to audition anyway.
And isn't he someone you know?

283
00:17:22,237 --> 00:17:26,625
- Isn't this a good thing?
- Exactly. So you took away his chance.

284
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:29,616
Without this, he could've earned
some other role on his own.

285
00:17:29,616 --> 00:17:33,300
Sometimes you give up one thing
to gain another.

286
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:35,397
You have to protect Yi Jae, right?

287
00:17:37,096 --> 00:17:40,675
What does Yi Jae have to do with this?

288
00:17:40,675 --> 00:17:45,559
What we need to do here is cast Sim Yu Geon...

289
00:17:45,559 --> 00:17:47,748
and protect Yi Jae.

290
00:17:47,748 --> 00:17:50,764
- In Uk!
- Ian, wake up.

291
00:17:50,764 --> 00:17:54,502
I don't care how many awards you've won
or how successful your debut was...

292
00:17:54,502 --> 00:17:56,304
This is only your second project.

293
00:17:56,304 --> 00:17:59,189
It's a period romance
that's already hard to finance...

294
00:17:59,189 --> 00:18:02,772
and co-directed
with an unproven newcomer. Hey...

295
00:18:02,772 --> 00:18:04,586
You're already getting
almost everything you wanted.

296
00:18:04,586 --> 00:18:06,993
Can't you give up this one thing?

297
00:18:10,653 --> 00:18:13,471
Without CEO An,

298
00:18:13,471 --> 00:18:16,731
we never would've gotten this far.

299
00:18:17,332 --> 00:18:20,525
Don't forget where we came from. Okay?

300
00:18:20,525 --> 00:18:22,255
You're right.

301
00:18:23,132 --> 00:18:25,635
You should've told me from the start...

302
00:18:25,635 --> 00:18:27,773
that people like us couldn't do this, Mr. Seo.

303
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:30,656
You said it had to be this project!

304
00:18:30,656 --> 00:18:34,308
What was I supposed to do?
You said it was your dream!

305
00:18:38,007 --> 00:18:40,828
You were only 22...

306
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:42,846
wandering around with nowhere to live,

307
00:18:42,846 --> 00:18:44,858
carrying nothing but that script
when you came to me.

308
00:18:44,858 --> 00:18:47,608
I still remember that day.

309
00:18:49,444 --> 00:18:53,091
Just like you're trying to keep
the promise you made to Yi Jae, I'm...

310
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:54,814
I'm just trying to keep
the promise I made to you.

311
00:18:54,814 --> 00:18:58,392
But I'm not capable of doing more yet,
so this is the best I can do.

312
00:19:04,068 --> 00:19:05,968
I'm sorry.

313
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:10,334
I'm sorry... sorry, Ian.

314
00:19:28,062 --> 00:19:31,392
Come on in. The food's getting cold.

315
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:40,266
Director Woo.

316
00:19:40,266 --> 00:19:42,604
I'm sure CEO Seo explained it.

317
00:19:43,306 --> 00:19:45,213
Give him the role...

318
00:19:45,213 --> 00:19:48,564
or drop Ju Yi Jae.

319
00:19:51,421 --> 00:19:54,540
You're set on backing Sim Yu Geon,

320
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:57,373
and I'm set on protecting Ju Yi Jae...

321
00:19:57,996 --> 00:20:00,638
Doesn't that already answer the question?

322
00:20:00,638 --> 00:20:01,989
I like how quick you are.

323
00:20:01,989 --> 00:20:04,809
Let's make one thing clear.

324
00:20:06,004 --> 00:20:07,777
This film...

325
00:20:08,489 --> 00:20:11,177
won't fall apart just because we lose
one investor like you, CEO An,

326
00:20:11,177 --> 00:20:15,608
but it cannot be made
without Director Ju Yi Jae.

327
00:20:15,608 --> 00:20:17,827
You decided to invest because of her script,

328
00:20:17,827 --> 00:20:22,142
so I'd appreciate it...
if you stopped telling us to keep or cut her.

329
00:20:25,308 --> 00:20:29,997
I only looked because it was
your next project. Otherwise...

330
00:20:29,997 --> 00:20:32,936
would it have ever made it onto my desk?

331
00:20:34,045 --> 00:20:37,675
Anyway, I got the answer I wanted,
so I'll be going now.

332
00:20:37,675 --> 00:20:40,281
Oh... you're leaving already?

333
00:20:40,281 --> 00:20:41,706
He has boxing practice.

334
00:20:41,706 --> 00:20:44,010
Even if we leave now,
he'll only get an hour in.

335
00:20:44,010 --> 00:20:45,684
Oh...

336
00:20:46,648 --> 00:20:48,682
What are you doing? Aren't you coming?

337
00:20:48,682 --> 00:20:50,347
Goodbye.

338
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:54,504
Oh, right!

339
00:20:54,504 --> 00:20:57,173
I heard you're already
looking for a top actress.

340
00:20:57,173 --> 00:21:00,386
Since I saved you the trouble of
finding your male lead,

341
00:21:00,386 --> 00:21:05,667
why not spend that time
finding the perfect female lead instead?

342
00:21:21,114 --> 00:21:23,860
- Oh? You're getting back from work, In Uk?
- Yeah.

343
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:26,004
Aren't you all dying to know
what In Uk does for a living?

344
00:21:26,004 --> 00:21:27,219
- Yeah.
- Right.

345
00:21:27,219 --> 00:21:30,195
Go change and come join us!
We were just about to play Truth or Dare!

346
00:21:30,195 --> 00:21:32,445
Oh... I'm exhausted.

347
00:21:32,445 --> 00:21:34,655
Have a good time.

348
00:21:35,884 --> 00:21:38,026
It's understandable to be tired...

349
00:21:38,026 --> 00:21:39,050
That's a shame.

350
00:21:39,050 --> 00:21:41,192
- Right.
- Right.

351
00:21:42,218 --> 00:21:46,056
Those two are heading to the terrace!
Stay on them!

352
00:22:10,484 --> 00:22:12,395
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

353
00:22:12,395 --> 00:22:14,704
<i>You look tired.</i>

354
00:22:56,768 --> 00:23:00,405
<i>Keep what we talked about earlier
a secret from Yi Jae.</i>

355
00:23:14,803 --> 00:23:17,206
You came, Yu Geon?

356
00:23:17,206 --> 00:23:21,109
What? Why do you look so cool today?

357
00:23:21,109 --> 00:23:23,491
Were you playing the handsome lead?

358
00:23:24,288 --> 00:23:26,289
Why are you here?

359
00:23:26,969 --> 00:23:29,334
Well... you weren't replying,

360
00:23:29,334 --> 00:23:33,342
and your motorcycle was outside,
so I thought you were home.

361
00:23:34,355 --> 00:23:37,611
By the way, is something wrong?

362
00:23:37,611 --> 00:23:40,290
You look exhausted.

363
00:23:40,290 --> 00:23:43,088
- I asked why you came.
- Oh!

364
00:23:44,015 --> 00:23:46,449
Give me your hand.

365
00:23:46,449 --> 00:23:48,711
Come on.

366
00:23:56,519 --> 00:24:00,243
Ta-da! I snuck this out of my mom's drawer.

367
00:24:00,243 --> 00:24:03,151
My voyage has officially begun.

368
00:24:03,151 --> 00:24:04,809
I did well, right?

369
00:24:09,446 --> 00:24:12,768
I hate...

370
00:24:12,768 --> 00:24:15,124
when you show up like this.

371
00:24:20,237 --> 00:24:21,714
Are you mad?

372
00:24:21,714 --> 00:24:23,338
Because I came without telling you?

373
00:24:23,338 --> 00:24:24,963
I'm sorry.

374
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:28,203
- Next time I'll...
- Let's stop being friends too.

375
00:24:30,101 --> 00:24:32,893
How could we ever be friends?

376
00:24:33,935 --> 00:24:37,316
Friends are people
who belong in the same world.

377
00:24:39,207 --> 00:24:40,813
Then...

378
00:24:42,579 --> 00:24:46,704
What have we been until now?

379
00:24:48,882 --> 00:24:52,408
Oh Ha Na... and Extra No. 1.

380
00:24:55,555 --> 00:24:57,311
Please leave.

381
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:23,775
[Expiration date: Ten thousand years]

382
00:25:51,638 --> 00:25:53,262
[Open Frame Works, Film Production]

383
00:26:00,252 --> 00:26:04,005
Wow... my stick-figure storyboard
turned into this?

384
00:26:04,005 --> 00:26:07,612
- Who drew these storyboards?
- Director Ian did them himself.

385
00:26:07,612 --> 00:26:09,246
Oh, he... I mean,

386
00:26:09,246 --> 00:26:11,711
Director Woo even draws his own storyboards?

387
00:26:11,711 --> 00:26:17,213
Yeah. He doesn't have a storyboard artist.
He usually draws the storyboards himself.

388
00:26:17,213 --> 00:26:21,347
No wonder... it was exactly how I imagined it.

389
00:26:25,205 --> 00:26:26,985
You're here.

390
00:26:26,985 --> 00:26:30,718
- Jenny, could you give us a minute?
- Yeah.

391
00:26:38,653 --> 00:26:42,035
- What's up?
- We're going to discuss this in the meeting...

392
00:26:42,035 --> 00:26:44,164
but I thought you should know beforehand.

393
00:26:44,164 --> 00:26:46,323
What is it?

394
00:26:46,323 --> 00:26:49,006
Sim Yu Geon has been...

395
00:26:49,006 --> 00:26:51,652
cast as Moo Gyeom. It's official.

396
00:26:51,652 --> 00:26:55,706
Yu Geon? That Sim Yu Geon I know? How?

397
00:26:55,706 --> 00:26:59,199
Wasn't he supposed to audition?
Did it already happen?

398
00:26:59,199 --> 00:27:02,057
Turns out Yu Geon signed with Topline.

399
00:27:03,414 --> 00:27:07,835
And as you know,
CEO An is our business partner...

400
00:27:07,835 --> 00:27:10,438
Sim Yu Geon signed with them?

401
00:27:10,438 --> 00:27:12,186
They must see a lot of potential in him.

402
00:27:12,186 --> 00:27:15,673
A company that big doesn't back just anyone.

403
00:27:15,673 --> 00:27:20,420
Wow... what's gotten into Yu Geon?
Best betrayal ever.

404
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:25,009
- You look really happy.
- Of course I am! This is amazing!

405
00:27:25,009 --> 00:27:27,226
But that's so fascinating.

406
00:27:27,226 --> 00:27:30,498
I guess when it's meant to happen,
it finds a way.

407
00:27:30,498 --> 00:27:33,401
As long as you're happy... it's fine.

408
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:36,104
Oh, sorry.

409
00:27:36,104 --> 00:27:38,643
I was only thinking about myself.
Are you okay with this?

410
00:27:38,643 --> 00:27:41,884
We were going to have Yu Geon audition anyway.

411
00:27:41,884 --> 00:27:44,772
- I'm happy too.
- Oh...

412
00:27:51,088 --> 00:27:52,778
Hello.

413
00:27:52,778 --> 00:27:54,656
You're here.

414
00:27:54,656 --> 00:27:57,733
- Take care.
- Good work.

415
00:28:04,476 --> 00:28:06,961
- Good work today.
- Good work.

416
00:28:06,961 --> 00:28:08,751
Good work today.

417
00:28:09,452 --> 00:28:13,486
Oh. Hey, Sim Yu Geon!

418
00:28:20,129 --> 00:28:25,301
Hey! Why the long face?
We should be throwing you a celebration!

419
00:28:26,133 --> 00:28:28,728
- I'm sorry, Yi Jae.
- What are you sorry for?

420
00:28:28,728 --> 00:28:30,709
I'm grateful you're playing our Moo Gyeom.

421
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:34,370
I know what this film means to you...

422
00:28:34,370 --> 00:28:36,783
I shouldn't have let it happen like this.

423
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:39,028
Yu Geon,

424
00:28:39,028 --> 00:28:41,175
that's life, you know.

425
00:28:41,175 --> 00:28:44,463
Sometimes a meteor just drops
right in front of you.

426
00:28:44,463 --> 00:28:47,531
You wonder if it could really belong to you,

427
00:28:47,531 --> 00:28:49,785
but if you pick it up, then it's yours.

428
00:28:49,785 --> 00:28:52,737
You grabbed this opportunity,
so stop shrinking away from it.

429
00:28:52,737 --> 00:28:55,250
Our Moo Gyeom isn't that kind of person.

430
00:28:57,844 --> 00:29:00,982
- Yi Jae...
- I'm not just trying to comfort you.

431
00:29:00,982 --> 00:29:04,330
I don't want you thinking you got this
only because of CEO An.

432
00:29:04,330 --> 00:29:06,187
Do Soo Bin and I look like pushovers?

433
00:29:06,187 --> 00:29:09,556
Do we seem like the type to say yes
to something we absolutely hate?

434
00:29:09,556 --> 00:29:11,775
No, but...

435
00:29:16,885 --> 00:29:21,033
Seriously, what's gotten into you?
Do I have to knock some sense into you?

436
00:29:24,608 --> 00:29:26,241
Yi Jae...

437
00:29:27,417 --> 00:29:32,608
I don't think I can be part of your film
while keeping this from you.

438
00:29:34,935 --> 00:29:37,288
<i>The door is opening.</i>

439
00:29:47,210 --> 00:29:49,925
<i>Soo Bin told me not to say anything.</i>

440
00:29:52,331 --> 00:29:56,090
<i>But... CEO An made a deal.</i>

441
00:29:56,090 --> 00:29:58,687
<i>She said if they didn't cast me as the lead,</i>

442
00:30:00,172 --> 00:30:02,886
<i>she'd remove you as director.</i>

443
00:30:02,886 --> 00:30:06,733
<i>Soo Bin accepted me to protect you.</i>

444
00:30:14,855 --> 00:30:16,898
Hey! Director Woo!

445
00:30:17,661 --> 00:30:18,962
I thought you went home.

446
00:30:18,962 --> 00:30:21,095
You should eat while you work.
I brought gimbap.

447
00:30:21,095 --> 00:30:24,295
I was getting hungry. Thanks.

448
00:30:33,129 --> 00:30:35,976
Did you meet with Yu Geon?

449
00:30:35,976 --> 00:30:38,539
Oh... yeah.

450
00:30:38,539 --> 00:30:43,914
He looked like a soaked puppy,
so I gave him a good talking-to!

451
00:30:43,914 --> 00:30:48,699
- He's talented. He'll do a great job.
- Yeah.

452
00:30:48,699 --> 00:30:50,807
I'll enjoy it.

453
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:52,970
Thank you.

454
00:30:52,970 --> 00:30:54,891
Oh, it looks so good.

455
00:30:55,739 --> 00:30:59,185
[Yu Geon's Dream]

456
00:31:09,194 --> 00:31:12,391
<i>I heard your father left this for Woo Soo Bin.</i>

457
00:31:12,391 --> 00:31:14,165
<i>He asked him to look after you, Yu Geon.</i>

458
00:31:14,165 --> 00:31:16,722
<i>If you were going to get in
through connections anyway,</i>

459
00:31:16,722 --> 00:31:19,652
<i>you should've done it back
when you were young enough to be naive.</i>

460
00:31:19,652 --> 00:31:22,756
<i>After everything you've put yourself through...
now, of all times?</i>

461
00:31:22,756 --> 00:31:25,360
<i>You've already lost the most important thing.</i>

462
00:31:25,360 --> 00:31:27,671
<i>I bought your heart.</i>

463
00:31:27,671 --> 00:31:29,730
<i>So you'll never fall in love with Ha Na.</i>

464
00:31:29,730 --> 00:31:33,522
<i>Ta-da! I snuck this out of my mom's drawer.</i>

465
00:31:33,522 --> 00:31:36,402
<i>My voyage has officially begun.</i>

466
00:31:36,402 --> 00:31:38,302
<i>I did well, right?</i>

467
00:32:04,925 --> 00:32:06,363
[Actor Sim Yu Geon]

468
00:32:11,468 --> 00:32:14,488
Why? Did something happen?

469
00:32:15,448 --> 00:32:16,954
<i>Dad...</i>

470
00:32:17,546 --> 00:32:20,355
Yeah, why? Did something happen?

471
00:32:22,008 --> 00:32:25,300
<i>I got... cast.</i>

472
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:28,503
<i>I'm the lead in a movie.</i>

473
00:32:34,233 --> 00:32:35,936
Really?

474
00:32:37,865 --> 00:32:40,120
Then why do you sound like that?

475
00:32:43,172 --> 00:32:45,072
<i>Because I'm happy.</i>

476
00:32:48,309 --> 00:32:50,032
Yeah?

477
00:32:50,032 --> 00:32:51,414
Good. You've worked hard.

478
00:32:51,414 --> 00:32:52,980
Let's hang up.

479
00:32:53,886 --> 00:32:55,436
<i>Dad!</i>

480
00:32:58,553 --> 00:33:00,453
<i>Thank you.</i>

481
00:33:30,390 --> 00:33:33,412
Are you sure you're okay staying at my place?

482
00:33:33,412 --> 00:33:36,411
If you ask me one more time, that'll make ten.

483
00:33:36,411 --> 00:33:38,953
Stop asking. I'm really fine.

484
00:33:38,953 --> 00:33:43,583
I can't believe someone like you
would come to such a humble place...

485
00:33:43,583 --> 00:33:47,549
When I shoot overseas,
I've stayed in much worse places.

486
00:33:47,549 --> 00:33:51,029
Give me a sleeping bag
and I can even sleep outside.

487
00:33:55,373 --> 00:33:58,416
I'll put the suitcase in quickly.

488
00:34:11,633 --> 00:34:13,996
Are you going somewhere?

489
00:34:13,996 --> 00:34:15,466
The New York shoot isn't until next week.

490
00:34:15,466 --> 00:34:20,809
You know next week's schedule,
but not that my contract ended?

491
00:34:20,809 --> 00:34:23,786
Since when have we ever worked
by the contract dates?

492
00:34:23,786 --> 00:34:25,934
I'm going independent.

493
00:34:25,934 --> 00:34:27,053
I'm not renewing.

494
00:34:27,053 --> 00:34:29,442
- What, are you retiring?
- No.

495
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:31,595
Why do you assume I'm quitting?

496
00:34:31,595 --> 00:34:33,432
Because you've never wanted to do it.

497
00:34:33,432 --> 00:34:37,930
I never even got the chance to find out!

498
00:34:38,568 --> 00:34:41,514
From now on, I'm living my own life.

499
00:34:41,514 --> 00:34:44,956
- Did you get everything loaded, Chae Yeon?
- Yeah.

500
00:34:46,753 --> 00:34:49,561
Thank you for everything, CEO An.

501
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:54,284
Is this because of Sim Yu Geon?

502
00:34:55,785 --> 00:35:00,394
You've been acting like a teenager.
Is it because of him?

503
00:35:00,394 --> 00:35:05,363
Jeez... how could you
fall for someone like him?

504
00:35:05,363 --> 00:35:07,117
Go see a therapist instead!

505
00:35:07,117 --> 00:35:08,249
- Mom!
- What!

506
00:35:08,249 --> 00:35:13,016
It's because of you!
You make me feel like I can't breathe!

507
00:35:13,016 --> 00:35:14,760
And you already dug into
Yu Geon's background again?

508
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:18,658
Oh, jeez... what do you take me for?

509
00:35:18,658 --> 00:35:22,940
You think I only look into people's pasts?
I look at their futures too.

510
00:35:22,940 --> 00:35:26,621
So stop acting up
and go clear your head for a couple of days.

511
00:35:26,621 --> 00:35:28,488
Gangneung should do.

512
00:35:28,488 --> 00:35:32,218
Chae Yeon, use the company card!
And don't let Ha Na eat sweets!

513
00:35:32,218 --> 00:35:33,963
Yes...

514
00:35:38,904 --> 00:35:42,398
Director Kang, announce Ha Na's hiatus.

515
00:35:42,398 --> 00:35:45,704
The reason? Make something.

516
00:35:53,072 --> 00:35:55,546
Ha Na, do we really have to go this far?

517
00:35:55,546 --> 00:35:57,233
Huh? That's Jaden.

518
00:35:57,233 --> 00:35:59,018
Who's that? Should we stop him?

519
00:35:59,018 --> 00:36:00,856
No, pass.

520
00:36:00,856 --> 00:36:02,653
He's a CEO now.

521
00:36:02,653 --> 00:36:05,385
CEOs can't be trusted as my mom can...

522
00:36:05,385 --> 00:36:06,987
Pass on the CEO!

523
00:36:06,987 --> 00:36:09,469
Ha Na! That's Director Ian!

524
00:36:09,469 --> 00:36:12,130
- Should we stop him? Should I go now?
- No, no!

525
00:36:12,130 --> 00:36:14,489
He's the last person we should approach.

526
00:36:14,489 --> 00:36:19,413
But he's directing "Gyeongseong Love Song."
Then who are we supposed to ask?

527
00:36:19,413 --> 00:36:20,902
Huh?

528
00:36:21,533 --> 00:36:23,242
That person!

529
00:36:23,875 --> 00:36:26,007
Ha Na, wait...

530
00:36:35,627 --> 00:36:37,767
Director Ju Yi Jae.

531
00:36:40,672 --> 00:36:42,457
Oh Ha Na?

532
00:36:44,381 --> 00:36:46,434
But how do you know me?

533
00:36:46,434 --> 00:36:49,620
I used to watch "Here comes Yi Jae."

534
00:36:49,620 --> 00:36:52,776
We even met at that
department store event. Right?

535
00:36:53,452 --> 00:36:57,445
Isn't this what you call... fate?

536
00:36:57,445 --> 00:36:59,042
Fate?

537
00:37:00,536 --> 00:37:03,665
Oh, what was it you wanted to tell me earlier?

538
00:37:04,570 --> 00:37:06,891
Please give me the script for
"Gyeongseong Love Song," Director.

539
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:10,966
Oh, I thought a copy
was already sent to CEO An.

540
00:37:10,966 --> 00:37:14,482
Exactly! I should've stolen it then!

541
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:15,904
Pardon?

542
00:37:16,543 --> 00:37:20,938
I really want to be in this film, Director.

543
00:37:20,938 --> 00:37:23,784
I've never wanted anything like this before.

544
00:37:23,784 --> 00:37:26,101
- Really?
- Yes...

545
00:37:27,364 --> 00:37:28,532
Can you hear her?

546
00:37:28,532 --> 00:37:31,892
Nan Young is alive inside me.

547
00:37:31,892 --> 00:37:33,332
Yes, I can hear her.

548
00:37:33,332 --> 00:37:35,727
Yes. I'll get it to you. How should I send it?

549
00:37:35,727 --> 00:37:38,216
Through your manager?

550
00:37:39,580 --> 00:37:42,062
Put your number in, Yi Jae.

551
00:37:42,062 --> 00:37:44,897
"Yi Jae..." "Yi Jae?"

552
00:37:44,897 --> 00:37:48,165
Is Oh Ha Na seriously asking for
my number right now?

553
00:37:48,165 --> 00:37:49,771
But...

554
00:37:49,771 --> 00:37:53,197
let's keep today our little secret.

555
00:37:53,197 --> 00:37:55,775
- Yes.
- Shh!

556
00:37:56,879 --> 00:37:59,335
[An Yoo Jeong]

557
00:37:59,335 --> 00:38:00,646
[Lim Min Ju]

558
00:38:00,646 --> 00:38:04,382
As expected, top stars
are booked two projects ahead.

559
00:38:04,382 --> 00:38:08,253
At least Actress Lim Min Ju might be
available if schedules work out.

560
00:38:08,253 --> 00:38:11,229
Well... what about Oh Ha Na?

561
00:38:11,958 --> 00:38:16,490
Oh... I heard she's in talks for another film.

562
00:38:16,490 --> 00:38:19,939
An article came out a few days ago saying
she's taking a break from acting.

563
00:38:19,939 --> 00:38:21,536
Really?

564
00:38:24,738 --> 00:38:27,292
[Actress Oh Ha Na]
<i>I'm here.</i>

565
00:38:27,292 --> 00:38:29,037
<i>Action!</i>

566
00:38:32,504 --> 00:38:33,863
- What?
- What?

567
00:38:33,863 --> 00:38:36,028
- You can't just come in here.
- Who are you?

568
00:38:36,028 --> 00:38:38,279
- Isn't that a rifle?
- Excuse me.

569
00:38:41,150 --> 00:38:42,819
Jeez, can't you see I'm in a meeting...

570
00:38:42,819 --> 00:38:45,240
- My comrades!
- Nan Young?

571
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:47,784
She actually came dressed like that?

572
00:38:47,784 --> 00:38:49,897
<i>This is no time to sit around!</i>

573
00:38:49,897 --> 00:38:55,516
<i>Nothing will change if we simply sit back
and discuss the situation at hand.</i>

574
00:38:55,516 --> 00:39:01,037
<i>Do you know what I thought
after I blew up Wolhajeong?</i>

575
00:39:01,037 --> 00:39:03,542
<i>"I have nowhere left to return to.</i>

576
00:39:03,542 --> 00:39:06,143
<i>I could only move forward.</i>

577
00:39:06,143 --> 00:39:08,521
<i>Sorrow is temporary...</i>

578
00:39:09,807 --> 00:39:12,787
<i>But joy lasts forever."</i>

579
00:39:24,133 --> 00:39:25,788
<i>That's right, Comrade Nan Young.</i>

580
00:39:25,788 --> 00:39:29,040
<i>Let's march toward independence together.</i>

581
00:39:37,091 --> 00:39:39,191
Why did you show up only now?

582
00:39:39,191 --> 00:39:42,955
Just like you said, Ha Na,
it felt like Na Young was alive again.

583
00:39:48,869 --> 00:39:50,769
Director Ju Yi Jae?

584
00:39:51,403 --> 00:39:53,034
Director?

585
00:39:54,007 --> 00:39:55,590
Yeah...

586
00:40:00,568 --> 00:40:05,252
I've also prepared Scene 34. May I continue?

587
00:40:05,252 --> 00:40:08,786
Ms. Oh Ha Na, what exactly are you doing?

588
00:40:08,786 --> 00:40:12,003
I'm confident I can play Na Young really well.

589
00:40:12,003 --> 00:40:15,388
- Please give me the chance! I'm begging you!
- Yes...

590
00:40:15,388 --> 00:40:17,220
You were good.

591
00:40:17,220 --> 00:40:20,056
But it was the same performance
I've always seen from you.

592
00:40:20,056 --> 00:40:22,590
I mean, it wasn't anything special.

593
00:40:24,100 --> 00:40:25,480
Then...

594
00:40:25,480 --> 00:40:30,867
may I tell you why you should
choose me specifically?

595
00:40:30,867 --> 00:40:33,043
Oh? I'd like to hear this.

596
00:40:35,184 --> 00:40:37,005
I...

597
00:40:38,181 --> 00:40:42,267
I know someone
whose life is just like Nan Young's.

598
00:40:42,267 --> 00:40:48,197
A child who only did what they were told,
never dreaming for themselves...

599
00:40:50,083 --> 00:40:54,295
Never even realizing
their whole world was just a tiny prison.

600
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:59,751
Then I met someone like Moo Gyeom and realized.

601
00:41:00,903 --> 00:41:04,693
<i>Here, you shoot the next take.</i>

602
00:41:07,090 --> 00:41:10,332
"Maybe if I break out of my little world,

603
00:41:10,332 --> 00:41:13,111
there's a much bigger one waiting for me."

604
00:41:13,111 --> 00:41:17,996
"I wanted to live in the same world as him."

605
00:41:19,510 --> 00:41:25,215
So they blew up their own little world
and ran out of it.

606
00:41:25,215 --> 00:41:27,244
I...

607
00:41:27,244 --> 00:41:30,712
walked away from Topline Entertainment.

608
00:41:30,712 --> 00:41:33,194
I don't have an agency now,

609
00:41:33,194 --> 00:41:35,949
and I plan to keep going on my own.

610
00:41:35,949 --> 00:41:40,698
I also personally asked
Director Ju Yi Jae for this script.

611
00:41:40,698 --> 00:41:41,744
Oh...

612
00:41:41,744 --> 00:41:45,190
Then CEO An has no idea about any of this?

613
00:41:45,190 --> 00:41:47,262
She doesn't.

614
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:53,148
So...

615
00:41:53,148 --> 00:41:55,045
even if I get the part,

616
00:41:55,045 --> 00:41:59,736
I'd like to keep it hidden
until filming starts.

617
00:41:59,736 --> 00:42:03,057
I'm sorry. Please help me...

618
00:42:03,057 --> 00:42:07,992
So I can live as Oh Ha Na, not her daughter.

619
00:42:10,703 --> 00:42:14,141
If Nan Young can be
my first step toward independence,

620
00:42:14,141 --> 00:42:17,304
it'll mean everything to me.

621
00:42:18,622 --> 00:42:23,697
After all, Nan Young's independence
has a happy ending.

622
00:42:27,568 --> 00:42:31,778
Could you wait outside for a moment?

623
00:42:42,673 --> 00:42:45,603
Sorry to keep you waiting. Please have a seat.

624
00:42:56,194 --> 00:42:57,979
Ms. Oh Ha Na.

625
00:43:01,727 --> 00:43:03,530
Let's do this together.

626
00:43:03,530 --> 00:43:06,007
I'm counting on you as our Nan Young.

627
00:43:08,055 --> 00:43:10,763
Oh, thank you.

628
00:43:10,763 --> 00:43:15,489
I'll do my absolute best
to become the best Nan Young I can.

629
00:43:15,489 --> 00:43:17,557
Do you know...

630
00:43:18,658 --> 00:43:21,256
why I rejected you before?

631
00:43:21,256 --> 00:43:22,852
Well, that's because...

632
00:43:22,852 --> 00:43:26,009
my English wasn't good enough.

633
00:43:26,009 --> 00:43:29,986
The biggest reason was your attitude, Ha Na.

634
00:43:30,686 --> 00:43:36,686
You looked like a kid dragged there by her mom.

635
00:43:37,427 --> 00:43:39,202
Oh...

636
00:43:39,202 --> 00:43:41,806
I knew I couldn't fool a director's eyes.

637
00:43:41,806 --> 00:43:44,432
But today was different.

638
00:43:45,038 --> 00:43:49,124
You were impressive...
and it made me excited to work with you.

639
00:43:51,092 --> 00:43:53,125
Thank you.

640
00:43:54,569 --> 00:43:56,136
Well, anyway,

641
00:43:56,136 --> 00:44:00,091
from now on, we'll contact you directly.

642
00:44:00,091 --> 00:44:01,983
Keeping this confidential is our top priority.

643
00:44:01,983 --> 00:44:04,434
So don't tell your co-star either.

644
00:44:04,434 --> 00:44:06,750
Oh, right. Moo Gyeom!

645
00:44:06,750 --> 00:44:09,026
So is he someone I know?

646
00:44:09,026 --> 00:44:10,830
Who is it?

647
00:44:22,744 --> 00:44:25,580
- I told you not to come...
- Why?

648
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:27,187
Why did you do it?

649
00:44:27,187 --> 00:44:29,827
Why did you sign a contract with my mom?

650
00:44:32,419 --> 00:44:34,805
Because I have to become someone.

651
00:44:35,892 --> 00:44:38,127
So please...

652
00:44:38,127 --> 00:44:40,900
stay away from me.

653
00:44:42,387 --> 00:44:44,525
That contract...

654
00:44:45,995 --> 00:44:49,015
came with a promise that I'd never

655
00:44:49,872 --> 00:44:52,346
fall in love with you.

656
00:44:54,876 --> 00:44:56,776
That's a lie.

657
00:44:59,051 --> 00:45:01,026
No way...

658
00:45:01,026 --> 00:45:03,930
What kind of contract is that?

659
00:45:03,930 --> 00:45:06,423
Did you ever...

660
00:45:06,423 --> 00:45:08,786
love me, Yu Geon?

661
00:45:11,545 --> 00:45:13,278
No.

662
00:45:14,462 --> 00:45:16,420
Then why?

663
00:45:18,504 --> 00:45:21,342
What did we even have between us?

664
00:45:23,211 --> 00:45:25,111
You're right...

665
00:45:26,748 --> 00:45:29,536
What exactly was there between us?

666
00:45:32,304 --> 00:45:34,854
Because I know there wasn't
anything on my side.

667
00:45:50,469 --> 00:45:52,604
You're right.

668
00:45:52,604 --> 00:45:55,816
Friends are supposed to be alike.

669
00:46:01,860 --> 00:46:04,634
I misjudged you.

670
00:46:43,551 --> 00:46:45,344
[Moo Gyeom]

671
00:46:45,344 --> 00:46:48,431
[At the end of the hallway,
Moo Gyeom comes into view among the crowd]

672
00:46:48,431 --> 00:46:49,850
[Hair tied in a topknot, robe strings loosened]

673
00:46:49,850 --> 00:46:51,865
[Commanding presence, confident movements.
No shaky hands]

674
00:47:00,181 --> 00:47:02,081
Yeah, Dad.

675
00:47:06,032 --> 00:47:07,595
I'm here.

676
00:47:07,595 --> 00:47:09,651
You're here?

677
00:47:09,651 --> 00:47:12,248
Why are you here by yourself?
Where's Ju Young Jae?

678
00:47:12,248 --> 00:47:14,601
I sent him to the market.

679
00:47:21,282 --> 00:47:22,888
Here.

680
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:26,577
- What is it?
- Make this delivery first.

681
00:47:26,577 --> 00:47:28,852
The address is attached.

682
00:47:37,858 --> 00:47:39,812
Delivery.

683
00:47:43,765 --> 00:47:45,946
- Soo Bin?
- Yeah.

684
00:47:45,946 --> 00:47:47,308
Come in.

685
00:47:47,308 --> 00:47:48,684
What are you doing here?

686
00:47:48,684 --> 00:47:51,532
I asked your dad to arrange this.

687
00:47:51,532 --> 00:47:52,584
Huh?

688
00:47:52,584 --> 00:47:55,209
[CEO: Seo In Uk, Open Frame Works,
Actress, Name: Oh Ha Na]

689
00:47:55,209 --> 00:47:58,192
- I look forward to working with you.
- Me too.

690
00:47:58,192 --> 00:48:00,135
Oh, you're here?

691
00:48:02,490 --> 00:48:04,372
You're here?

692
00:48:05,089 --> 00:48:06,588
You two know each other?

693
00:48:06,588 --> 00:48:10,224
Yes, we knew each other. In the past...

694
00:48:10,224 --> 00:48:12,885
Oh, because of "Contract Marriage?"

695
00:48:12,885 --> 00:48:15,118
We were the lead and Extra No. 1,

696
00:48:15,118 --> 00:48:17,269
weren't we?

697
00:48:17,269 --> 00:48:18,577
What's going on here?

698
00:48:18,577 --> 00:48:20,381
We're here for the script reading.

699
00:48:20,381 --> 00:48:24,819
Say hello. That's Nan Young,
and he's Moo Gyeom.

700
00:48:24,819 --> 00:48:29,174
- What?
- Did Moo Gyeom sign the contract yet?

701
00:48:29,174 --> 00:48:32,112
Oh, maybe my mom signed it on your behalf, huh?

702
00:48:32,112 --> 00:48:35,530
Right... did you?

703
00:48:35,530 --> 00:48:38,908
That didn't sound like a question.

704
00:48:48,047 --> 00:48:49,953
Scene 47. Street. Night.

705
00:48:49,953 --> 00:48:55,004
"In the midst of it all, Na Young and
Moo Gyeom walk in, dressed in suits.

706
00:48:55,004 --> 00:48:57,962
Unlike the noise around them,
the two walk at a slow pace."

707
00:48:57,962 --> 00:49:00,793
"No matter how I look at you,
I see not a trace of worry."

708
00:49:00,793 --> 00:49:02,453
"How is it?

709
00:49:02,453 --> 00:49:07,232
Not Wolhajeong's lanterns,
but this moonlight reveals my beauty."

710
00:49:07,232 --> 00:49:10,166
"How is it that you find everything a jest?"

711
00:49:10,166 --> 00:49:13,852
To "Gyeongseong Love Song!"

712
00:49:21,798 --> 00:49:24,628
Oh, you two are so awkward.

713
00:49:24,628 --> 00:49:27,969
You're about to fall in love.
How about getting a little friendlier?

714
00:49:27,969 --> 00:49:30,965
I'd love that.

715
00:49:30,965 --> 00:49:33,754
But I'm just not sure if Yu Geon can.

716
00:49:33,754 --> 00:49:37,526
He seems cold, but he's a genuinely good guy.

717
00:49:37,526 --> 00:49:39,108
Really?

718
00:49:39,108 --> 00:49:42,673
I guess you're very different on the inside
than you are on the outside.

719
00:49:43,868 --> 00:49:48,016
Neither of you was bad,
but you barely looked at each other.

720
00:49:48,016 --> 00:49:49,681
Even if it's just a reading,

721
00:49:49,681 --> 00:49:52,429
you need to make eye contact
and build chemistry.

722
00:49:52,429 --> 00:49:55,673
If you're just going to read separately,
you could've done that at home.

723
00:49:56,314 --> 00:49:57,459
I'm sorry.

724
00:49:57,459 --> 00:49:59,137
I'm sorry.

725
00:49:59,137 --> 00:50:01,339
But that's what made it fascinating.

726
00:50:01,339 --> 00:50:04,325
How did you have such natural back-and-forth
without even looking at each other?

727
00:50:04,325 --> 00:50:06,680
Did you two have a falling-out or something?

728
00:50:13,797 --> 00:50:15,554
Guess I was right.

729
00:50:15,554 --> 00:50:17,637
Huh? They have to be friends first
to have a falling-out.

730
00:50:17,637 --> 00:50:19,555
I've seen those two together before.

731
00:50:19,555 --> 00:50:22,162
- They seemed pretty close.
- Oh, really?

732
00:50:22,162 --> 00:50:24,879
If the friendship's over,

733
00:50:24,879 --> 00:50:26,644
maybe it's time to fall in love instead.

734
00:50:26,644 --> 00:50:30,694
This is a romance.
You can't act like sworn enemies.

735
00:50:30,694 --> 00:50:32,866
Once the cameras roll, it'll be different.

736
00:50:32,866 --> 00:50:36,200
Love will be even harder.

737
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:38,341
You tell me.

738
00:50:39,059 --> 00:50:41,495
Can you love me?

739
00:50:49,341 --> 00:50:52,985
I have to. The directors told us to.

740
00:50:52,985 --> 00:50:55,104
What about you, Ha Na?

741
00:50:55,770 --> 00:51:00,589
If it helps the project,
I'll do whatever it takes.

742
00:51:01,209 --> 00:51:03,642
That's disappointing.

743
00:51:03,642 --> 00:51:06,221
I'm already in love.

744
00:51:14,700 --> 00:51:17,023
There's definitely something going on.

745
00:51:17,023 --> 00:51:19,690
- I'm dying to know. Right?
- Not really.

746
00:51:19,690 --> 00:51:23,081
Hey, I've never seen
Yu Geon look like that before.

747
00:51:23,081 --> 00:51:24,434
How should I put it...

748
00:51:24,434 --> 00:51:27,096
His eyes looked cold, yet... sad?

749
00:51:27,096 --> 00:51:29,462
Looks more like a breakup than a falling-out.

750
00:51:29,462 --> 00:51:32,285
That's good. It means
they've already been in love.

751
00:51:32,285 --> 00:51:33,736
What? Seriously?

752
00:51:33,736 --> 00:51:36,231
Then the emotions should come naturally.

753
00:51:36,231 --> 00:51:38,561
Should we shoot the breakup scene first?

754
00:51:38,561 --> 00:51:44,669
Wow... that was a terrible thing to say.

755
00:51:44,669 --> 00:51:47,218
Don't worry so much.

756
00:51:47,218 --> 00:51:49,996
On set, those feelings will slip out
whether they want them to or not.

757
00:51:49,996 --> 00:51:52,966
All we have to do is catch it and bring it out.

758
00:51:52,966 --> 00:51:57,683
Then maybe a love
that's like a war is better, right?

759
00:51:57,683 --> 00:52:02,005
I always wrote better in intense relationships
than peaceful ones.

760
00:52:02,005 --> 00:52:05,026
Probably because the emotions run deeper...

761
00:52:06,844 --> 00:52:08,095
When?

762
00:52:08,095 --> 00:52:09,483
Huh?

763
00:52:11,480 --> 00:52:14,730
I mean... back in college.
Most people date a classmate at least once.

764
00:52:14,730 --> 00:52:16,579
I didn't.

765
00:52:17,418 --> 00:52:19,423
Really?

766
00:52:19,423 --> 00:52:22,104
Come on, that's the perfect age for it.

767
00:52:22,104 --> 00:52:23,339
So what were you doing?

768
00:52:23,339 --> 00:52:25,915
Busy hauling equipment around on set.

769
00:52:25,915 --> 00:52:28,580
I'd buy one baguette
and make it last a whole week.

770
00:52:28,580 --> 00:52:33,006
Okay, enough! Skip it!
Is that even love at that age?

771
00:52:36,108 --> 00:52:38,210
Then what were we back then?

772
00:52:41,657 --> 00:52:44,722
When we were 18 and 19...

773
00:52:44,722 --> 00:52:46,641
what were we back then?

774
00:52:55,546 --> 00:52:57,651
It was love.

775
00:52:58,258 --> 00:53:01,715
Back then, too... When we were 18 and 19.

776
00:53:04,365 --> 00:53:06,473
And I think...

777
00:53:07,646 --> 00:53:09,896
it still is.

778
00:53:25,856 --> 00:53:28,085
I know everything.

779
00:53:28,085 --> 00:53:31,795
I know you accepted Yu Geon to protect me.

780
00:53:38,406 --> 00:53:40,923
- Yi Jae...
- I'm not blaming you.

781
00:53:40,923 --> 00:53:43,177
I don't blame you anymore.

782
00:53:43,789 --> 00:53:48,627
I just... kept wondering

783
00:53:48,627 --> 00:53:51,433
what kind of feeling that must've been.

784
00:53:52,499 --> 00:53:56,237
They say all great things begin
with something small.

785
00:53:56,237 --> 00:54:01,708
Just like loving me made you love filmmaking.

786
00:54:02,823 --> 00:54:05,082
But...

787
00:54:05,082 --> 00:54:07,888
isn't that feeling itself

788
00:54:07,888 --> 00:54:10,437
what makes it truly great?

789
00:54:10,437 --> 00:54:13,005
Even the heart...

790
00:54:13,005 --> 00:54:15,265
that made you decide to stop.

791
00:54:21,941 --> 00:54:24,470
Your heart is too big for me

792
00:54:24,470 --> 00:54:27,768
to keep pretending I don't see it, Woo Soo Bin.

793
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:31,732
So...

794
00:54:33,425 --> 00:54:35,325
don't stop.

795
00:55:19,161 --> 00:55:22,824
I'm already so nervous. What should I do?

796
00:55:22,824 --> 00:55:26,156
Even legendary directors get nervous
the night before their first shoot.

797
00:55:26,156 --> 00:55:27,169
Yeah?

798
00:55:27,169 --> 00:55:29,547
- That's why I come here the day before...
- Yeah.

799
00:55:29,547 --> 00:55:33,801
and run through everything in my head.

800
00:55:33,801 --> 00:55:35,181
How?

801
00:55:35,181 --> 00:55:36,618
Look.

802
00:55:36,618 --> 00:55:40,877
The first thing you'll notice
is probably the art department.

803
00:55:40,877 --> 00:55:44,132
- Yeah.
- They'll check all the signs again

804
00:55:45,478 --> 00:55:50,017
and set up the gukbap place nicely,
with the soup steaming.

805
00:55:50,017 --> 00:55:51,497
- Over there, Director of Photography...
- Yeah.

806
00:55:51,497 --> 00:55:55,345
will be waiting with gummies,
wondering when the setup will be finished.

807
00:55:55,345 --> 00:55:58,775
Yes, Assistant Director! I'm on my way!

808
00:55:59,649 --> 00:56:01,997
On set, always watch where you're stepping.

809
00:56:01,997 --> 00:56:04,615
Tripping over a cable can be a disaster.

810
00:56:04,615 --> 00:56:08,182
And stay out of the lighting crew's way.

811
00:57:12,679 --> 00:57:14,316
Yi Jae!

812
00:57:18,298 --> 00:57:20,537
And this...

813
00:57:20,537 --> 00:57:23,048
Director Ju Yi Jae, this is your spot.

814
00:57:23,048 --> 00:57:24,684
[Director Ju Yi Jae]

815
00:57:44,209 --> 00:57:46,666
[Director Ju Yi Jae]

816
00:57:50,016 --> 00:57:53,186
Sit here and call it out as loud as you can,

817
00:57:53,186 --> 00:57:57,284
"Ready... Action!"

818
00:57:57,284 --> 00:57:59,429
- Me?
- Yeah.

819
00:57:59,429 --> 00:58:03,409
[Director Woo Soo Bin, Director Ju Yi Jae]

820
00:58:03,409 --> 00:58:08,193
Everyone will be waiting for your cue.

821
00:58:11,200 --> 00:58:12,836
Go ahead.

822
00:58:24,090 --> 00:58:26,074
Ready...

823
00:58:34,343 --> 00:58:36,013
Action!

824
00:59:08,709 --> 00:59:09,901
[No Dating on Set]
<i>Directors,</i>

825
00:59:09,901 --> 00:59:12,515
<i>if you ever catch the staff dating,
report it to us right away.</i>

826
00:59:12,515 --> 00:59:15,993
<i>You should've stayed right by my side
and shown my mom properly.</i>

827
00:59:15,993 --> 00:59:17,640
<i>That there's absolutely no such thing as love.</i>

828
00:59:17,640 --> 00:59:18,792
<i>Relax.</i>

829
00:59:18,792 --> 00:59:21,301
<i>Oh Ha Na! Everyone, stop filming!</i>

830
00:59:21,301 --> 00:59:22,622
<i>I'll withdraw from the project, CEO An.</i>

831
00:59:22,622 --> 00:59:25,693
<i>It all happened because of
that stupid rebellious attitude of yours.</i>

832
00:59:25,693 --> 00:59:27,870
<i>I'm sorry. Because of me...</i>

833
00:59:27,870 --> 00:59:29,999
<i>I shouldn't have tried to fix you.</i>

834
00:59:29,999 --> 00:59:34,665
<i>Things that are broken once
are hard to fix completely.</i>

835
00:59:34,665 --> 00:59:36,388
<i>Yi Jae!</i>
